---
/* Four witnesses, divergent counts.
   Research question: did any two sources agree on what 長恨 contained?
   Bars run from zero — the counts really are close, and the honest finding is
   that they cluster without ever coinciding. Three encodings keep incomparable
   evidence from looking comparable:
     · solid        — a full item-level listing
     · hatched      — an issue-level count only; cannot be checked item by item
     · dashed tail  — a partial reading; the remainder is unattested, not absent
   The edition's own bar carries two stops because it counts at two levels. */
import j from '../data/janghan.json';

const X0 = 208, XW = 470, MAX = 56;
const x = (n) => X0 + (n / MAX) * XW;
const ROW = 40, PAD = 30;

const panels = [
  {
    key: 'issue1', label: '창간호 · Issue 1', head: 'January 1927',
    rows: [
      { name: 'Published bibliography', unit: 'articles', n: j.literature.issue1, kind: 'issue-level' },
      { name: 'Yonsei catalogue', unit: 'entries', n: j.yonsei.issue1, kind: 'full' },
      { name: '1927 table of contents', unit: 'items listed', n: j.toc_1927_attested, kind: 'partial', of: j.issue1.items },
      { name: 'This edition', unit: 'editorial units / textual items', n: j.issue1.units, n2: j.issue1.items, kind: 'edition' },
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'issue2', label: '2월호 · Issue 2', head: 'February 1927',
    rows: [
      { name: 'Published bibliography', unit: 'articles', n: j.literature.issue2, kind: 'issue-level' },
      { name: 'Yonsei catalogue', unit: 'entries', n: j.yonsei.issue2, kind: 'full' },
      { name: '1927 table of contents', unit: 'no 1927 scan survives', n: 0, kind: 'absent' },
      { name: 'This edition', unit: 'editorial units / textual items', n: j.issue2.units, n2: j.issue2.items, kind: 'edition' },
    ],
  },
];

let y = 8;
const laid = panels.map((p) => {
  const top = y;
  y += 34;
  const rows = p.rows.map((r) => { const ry = y; y += ROW; return { ...r, y: ry }; });
  y += PAD;
  return { ...p, top, rows };
});
const H = y;

const aria = panels.map((p) =>
  `${p.label}: ` + p.rows.map((r) =>
    r.kind === 'absent' ? `${r.name}, none — ${r.unit}`
    : r.kind === 'edition' ? `${r.name}, ${r.n} ${r.unit}`
    : r.kind === 'partial' ? `${r.name}, ${r.n} of ${r.of} attested`
    : `${r.name}, ${r.n} ${r.unit}`).join('; ')
).join('. ');
---
<figure id="fig-witnesses">
  <div class="fig-head">
    <span class="fig-no">Figure 1 · Four witnesses</span>
    <p class="fig-title">
      No two sources divide 長恨 the same way — and they are not counting the same kind of thing
    </p>
  </div>
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 760 ${H}`} role="img" aria-label={`Grouped bar chart. ${aria}.`}>
    <defs>
      <pattern id="jh-hatch" width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)">
        <rect width="6" height="6" fill="var(--paper)" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="6" stroke="var(--b4)" stroke-width="2.6" opacity="0.75" />
      </pattern>
    </defs>

    {laid.map((p) => (
      <>
        <text x="0" y={p.top + 14} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">
          {p.label}
        </text>
        <text x={X0} y={p.top + 14} font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="11.5"
          letter-spacing="1.1" fill="var(--muted)">{p.head.toUpperCase()}</text>
        <line x1="0" y1={p.top + 22} x2="760" y2={p.top + 22} stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1" />

        {p.rows.map((r) => (
          <>
            <text x="0" y={r.y + 15} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="13.5"
              fill={r.kind === 'edition' ? 'var(--ink)' : 'var(--muted)'}
              font-weight={r.kind === 'edition' ? '600' : '400'}>{r.name}</text>

            {r.kind === 'absent' ? (
              <>
                <line x1={X0} y1={r.y + 11} x2={X0 + 26} y2={r.y + 11}
                  stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="3" />
                <text x={X0 + 36} y={r.y + 15} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="12.5" fill="var(--faint)">
                  {r.unit}
                </text>
              </>
            ) : r.kind === 'edition' ? (
              <>
                <rect x={X0} y={r.y} width={x(r.n) - X0} height="22" fill="var(--ink)" rx="1.5" />
                <rect x={x(r.n)} y={r.y} width={x(r.n2) - x(r.n)} height="22" fill="var(--ink)" opacity="0.34" rx="1.5" />
                <text x={x(r.n2) + 10} y={r.y + 16} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">
                  {r.n} / {r.n2}
                </text>
                <text x={X0 + 6} y={r.y + 36} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--faint)">
                  {r.unit}
                </text>
              </>
            ) : r.kind === 'issue-level' ? (
              <>
                <rect x={X0} y={r.y} width={x(r.n) - X0} height="22" fill="url(#jh-hatch)"
                  stroke="var(--b4)" stroke-width="1" rx="1.5" />
                <text x={x(r.n) + 10} y={r.y + 16} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14" fill="var(--ink)">{r.n}</text>
                <text x={X0 + 6} y={r.y + 36} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--faint)">
                  {r.unit} · issue-level count only
                </text>
              </>
            ) : r.kind === 'partial' ? (
              <>
                <rect x={X0} y={r.y} width={x(r.n) - X0} height="22" fill="var(--b4)" opacity="0.62" rx="1.5" />
                <rect x={x(r.n)} y={r.y} width={x(r.of) - x(r.n)} height="22" fill="none"
                  stroke="var(--b4)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 3" opacity="0.6" rx="1.5" />
                <text x={x(r.of) + 10} y={r.y + 16} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14" fill="var(--ink)">
                  {r.n}<tspan fill="var(--faint)" font-size="12"> of {r.of}</tspan>
                </text>
                <text x={X0 + 6} y={r.y + 36} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--faint)">
                  attested by direct reading · the rest unlisted or illegible, not absent
                </text>
              </>
            ) : (
              <>
                <rect x={X0} y={r.y} width={x(r.n) - X0} height="22" fill="var(--b4)" opacity="0.62" rx="1.5" />
                <text x={x(r.n) + 10} y={r.y + 16} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14" fill="var(--ink)">{r.n}</text>
                <text x={X0 + 6} y={r.y + 36} font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--faint)">
                  {r.unit}
                </text>
              </>
            )}
          </>
        ))}
      </>
    ))}
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    Counts as each witness gives them, drawn from zero on a common scale. The three encodings mark evidence
    that cannot be compared like for like: <b>hatched</b> — the published bibliography counts at issue level,
    so it can never be checked item by item; <b>dashed</b> — the 1927 table of contents is a curated selection
    on a degraded scan, and {j.toc_1927_attested} of {j.issue1.items} items are attested in it by direct
    reading, the remainder unlisted rather than missing; <b>two-tone</b> — this edition counts at two levels at
    once, {j.issue1.units + j.issue2.units} editorial units containing {j.issue1.items + j.issue2.items}
    textual items. The witnesses cluster but never coincide, and the reason is structural, not careless: see
    Figure 2.
  </figcaption>

  <details class="chart-table">
    <summary>Data table</summary>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Witness</th><th scope="col">Issue</th><th scope="col">Count</th>
          <th scope="col">Counts what</th><th scope="col">Evidential status</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {laid.map((p) => p.rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{r.name}</td>
              <td>{p.label}</td>
              <td class="num">{r.kind === 'absent' ? '—' : r.kind === 'edition' ? `${r.n} / ${r.n2}` : r.n}</td>
              <td>{r.unit}</td>
              <td>{
                r.kind === 'issue-level' ? 'Issue-level only — not verifiable item by item'
                : r.kind === 'partial' ? `Partial reading — ${r.n} of ${r.of} attested`
                : r.kind === 'absent' ? 'No witness survives'
                : r.kind === 'edition' ? 'Editorial units / textual items'
                : 'Full item-level listing'
              }</td>
            </tr>
          )))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
</figure>
